{"candidates":[{"content":"The adjudication-ritual flag (§11.3) is sustained because the verdict-shape imposes an impossible joint requirement: it mandates that every surviving candidate satisfy both soundness and frontier-relevance simultaneously, a condition that cannot be reliably met under finite evidence, causing persistent failure.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"b8a37785307c04b68e61a7bba7c641d956b06d155e19b732efbc143c1fb218da"},{"role":"dependence","target":"6b0cb63c1fb6b1b7ce426c2a55832739f92a0551b82931ec95f43b497c5cc8c9"}],"typicality":0.85},{"content":"The flag is sustained by design as a stabilizing negative-feedback loop that prevents premature closure; the ritual deliberately maintains a high adjudicatory bar so that the system avoids settling on under-supported conjectures.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"033eab748c73445d9f6c9268a3fc8a1d604b7cb444a4274791ad0653653383a7"}],"typicality":0.75},{"content":"The §11.3 flag persists because of a type confusion in the critic harness: it conflates a meta-level judgment (the verdict is sound and relevant) with an object-level judgment (the candidate itself is sound and relevant), causing the ritual to reject verdicts for properties they only describe.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"f71bce81c0f3a0155c972e9512869e9d026abdddd3dc46bc9397d83a100f8745"},{"role":"dependence","target":"dfcc562d97853b4679aed7d501b01cff7e568cddb386fb1658df9f547a200d21"}],"typicality":0.65},{"content":"The flag is an artifact of temporal misalignment between two critic phases: 'sound and relevant' affirmations are registered before the frontier-exclusion check completes, so the system records both success and failure for the same candidate, sustaining a spurious flag.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"843cefb9d510742355b505ed529b2645d090eb0e54152a8eb7715ef4dcafb44b"},{"role":"dependence","target":"f71bce81c0f3a0155c972e9512869e9d026abdddd3dc46bc9397d83a100f8745"}],"typicality":0.6},{"content":"The flag is sustained because the two critics, frontier-claim-honest and frontier-above-floor, are redundant probes of the same latent quality; their near-collinear signals create a systematic covariance that the harness misreads as independent disagreement, blocking convergence.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"6b0cb63c1fb6b1b7ce426c2a55832739f92a0551b82931ec95f43b497c5cc8c9"}],"typicality":0.55},{"content":"The flag persists because the critics are adversarial validators operating under a covering principle of mutual exclusion at the frontier: any candidate that survives the soundness critic is necessarily pushed below the frontier by the relevance critic, making sustained failure structural rather than accidental.","evidence_refs":[],"refs":[{"role":"dependence","target":"dfcc562d97853b4679aed7d501b01cff7e568cddb386fb1658df9f547a200d21"},{"role":"dependence","target":"b8a37785307c04b68e61a7bba7c641d956b06d155e19b732efbc143c1fb218da"}],"typicality":0.7}],"simulation_proposals":[]}